  "text": "Independent Events Independent Events Events A and B are independent events if the probability of Event B occurring is the same whether or not Event A occurs. For example, if you throw two dice, the probability that the second die comes up 1 is independent of whether the first die came up 1. Formally, this can be stated in terms of conditional probabilities : P(A|B) = P(A) and P(B|A) = P(B).",
